Understanding Salesforce Data Structure

     Salesforce uses a Relational Database structure. This means data isn't just sitting in isolated lists; everything is connected through "Relationships."

     1. Master-Detail & Lookup Relationships:
             These are the technical links that connect one object to another. For example, a "Contact" record is       linked to an "Account" record so you know exactly which company a person works for.

     2. The "Single Source of Truth":
             Because of this structure, you only have to update a piece of information in one place (like a phone       number), and it updates everywhere that record is referenced across the system.

     3. Schema:
             This refers to the overall "map" of how all these objects and fields fit together.
